      "id": 1,
      "text": "Medford was incorporated as a township on March 1, 1847, after a local referendum split it from Evesham Township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medford%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By the 1880s, the Medford Glass Works—also known as Star Glass—employed about 250 workers at its peak.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medford%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Medford Historical Society preserves the 1857 Cross Keys One‑Room Schoolhouse, a rare example of 19th‑century rural education.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.medfordhistory.org/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Kirby’s Mill, a historic grist mill, earned a spot on the National Register of Historic Places and now hosts community events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medford%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Camden and Atlantic Railroad ran through Medford after the Civil War, fueling rapid commercial growth in the late 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medford%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Every summer, the Medford Historical Society stages its annual Quilt Show at Kirby’s Mill, showcasing local artisans and historic textiles.",
